# Smoke test for pc_resource. Two screenshots:
# - 01_initial: post-init / pre-action. The first process tick has
#   already fetched (via the socket fixture in
#   test/fixtures/socket/0.0.0.0.txt) but display_pc_resource was
#   called with the all-zero defaults BEFORE the synchronous handler
#   updated run_data, so gauges show 0%/0°C/etc.
# - 02_with_data: after `action UP` re-runs process which now reads
#   the parsed CPU 45 / 65°C / GPU 35 / RAM 50 / NET 100/500 KB/s.
#
# wait_ms 400 between action UP and screenshot 02_with_data: the
# default tick_for(50) the harness applies after each action step
# is too tight for pc_resource's 4-arc + multi-label layout to settle
# deterministically — runs were occasionally diffing 2-3% (over the
# 0.5% golden tolerance) when LVGL's render cadence didn't align
# perfectly with the screenshot tick. 400ms matches the cadence
# bilibili / stockmarket use after their action+screenshot pairs.

app pc_resource
# 02_with_data has subpixel-level non-determinism on the FontAwesome
# net-speed glyphs even after the wait_ms 400 padding (rerun #25102335574
# diffed 2.4% on what was a clean rerun the next attempt). Allow up to
# 3% so transient render variance doesn't false-fail CI; a real
# regression in the pc_resource_gui values would still exceed this.
threshold 3.0

wait_ms 1200
screenshot 01_initial
assert_no_crash

action UP
wait_ms 400
screenshot 02_with_data
assert_no_crash

action RETURN
wait_ms 200
assert_no_crash
